Z||000005||CUTTER||06-02-2000||04:14 AM||||Heck, My blue dingy thing is haunted. I riped that thing out a while ago when it was ringing at weird times. Like right when im hanging out with my friends (parked beside each other) I would start talking it would ring. Then stop, then I would start talking it would ring again, thats when i took it out. HECK....I WILL PAY YOU TO TAKE MY BLUE DINGY HAUNTING THINGY OFF MY HANDS!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  LOL   .....and the wierd thing is I still have the freakin thing in my room!<p>[This message has been edited by CUTTER (edited 06-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||06-02-2000||04:23 AM||||Hey Cutter, mine used to do the same thing!!! Like when I was driving down the road it would start to ding - I was waiting for the flight attendant to announce, "The Captain has now turned off the fasten seatbelt sign and you are free to move about the cabin"!!!<P>funny thing is, now it works fine and I have no clue what I did to make it work right - maybe the language directed at it late at night scared it!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||lawrence||06-02-2000||08:04 AM||||WhiteFieroBlur, and all,<P>I have a circuit that will convert the front turn signals to Daytime Running Lights (DRL).  This is a very simple circuit, so if you can solder, you can probably build a pair of modules for your car.  And since there are only a few parts, you don't even need a printed circuit board.  You can just solder the parts to the relay connections.<P>If interested, see: <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/1/we.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/99/1/we.htm</A> <P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine<p>[This message has been edited by lawrence (edited 06-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||WhiteFieroBlur||06-02-2000||09:30 AM||||Well I looked where the blue dingy box should be and I didn't see anything blue. All I saw was and I am about to go pre school on this description  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But I saw that big black box underneath and next to it was a lil small box connected with a white box and silver round thingy above it and next to it behind the little light bulb is a big space of nothing? So was the blue box supposed to go in the far right corner? I guess if it was taken out, its a sign that I shouldn't want one back huh? <P>  I just don't wanna be left out like if I am on a date and your date keeps looking at you funny cause she hears the dinging and finally runs out the car screaming.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||stsmithgt||06-02-2000||11:04 AM||||Your blue dingy thingy is going off while driving down the road?  You might check the sensor on your parking brake.  It can set that sucker off. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> My parking brake tends to stick a little and that was wearing out my rear brakes from them dragging.  I put that dinging thing in there and it reminds me to lube that cable AND to turn off my kewl cruising parking lights.||||reg||10
Z||000010||tgowens||06-02-2000||01:12 PM||||ok WhiteFieroBlur, this is for you......here is where the 'blue dingy thingy' fits...... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Blue_Dingy_Thingy.jpg">  (stsmithgt, the flight attendant took the picture, she was sitting in the passenger seat)........and, here is a closer picture showing the placement of all the thingys....... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Blue_Dingy_Thingy_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||06-02-2000||02:10 PM||||The white rectangular thingy (love these technical terms <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) is the flasher for the hazards and the round metal thingy is the flasher for the turn signals.  If the sub thingy dings, you need a new speaker and if the heater thingy dings, you're car is haunted.  Please bringy it to me and I'll fix it for you.  (Of course you'll need to sign it over to me 1st.  That's the only way it'll work.)||||reg||1
