Z||000018||Monkeyman||06-03-2000||10:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>those are the technical terms right outta the manual!! -- only a Hoosier would want me to sign over something to him -- if you work on it for me will it still go 'dingy' or will it then be a blue squeaky thingy? (you haven't explained the modification process to me yet........) -- the sub thingy buzzes and the heater thingy clunks but other than that, everything works fine. (the dash pocket whistles "the IU fight song" when I go over a railroad track - is that an indication of imminent failure??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hoosier and proud of it! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  It won't matter if it even makes a sound once I get done with it.  I'm not so good at signing my name so I don't think I'd be able to sign the title back over to you. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  And the IU fight song is not in indication of failure unless you're Bobby Knight!  (Go IU!)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Raydar||06-03-2000||11:48 AM||||Okay, for the truly "geek-inclined" among us. <BR>The blue dingy thingy can be <I>modified</I>. It's really easy to take apart. Each tone is produced by a voltage (or a ground) on one of the pins on the connector.  <BR>Anyway, you can change the pitch of the dings, as well as the repetition rate, by bridging the resistors & capacitors in the blue dingy thingy. It's too small to sound like a grandfather clock, or anything like that, but it *did* sound like a mantle clock.<BR>Instead of "dingdingdingding", you got "bong... bong... bong..." <BR>The "blue dingy thingy" became a "blue bong thingy". <BR>Not to be confused with a "brass bong thingy", or a "glass bong thingy". <BR>But that's a topic for another thread. Or another forum. <BR>If anybody's interested, I'll post a how-to.||||reg||6
Z||000020||Fret Naught||06-03-2000||02:33 PM||||Up until yesterday, I hated that blue dingy thingy, on my way home, I spied a bee buzzing around my neck on the rear window. Bees and I have a thing, I don't like them and they don't like me, everytime I get stung I have to shoot up this stuff from a little kit I carry. any way screaching to an immediate stop and bailing out of my car letting the bee escape, I inadvertantly bumped the light switch and turned on the running lights. when I got home that dam dingy thingy kept dinging. until I noticed the lights were on. Whew! I could of had a dead battery!! thanks dingy||||reg||1
Z||000021||Raydar||06-03-2000||10:35 PM||||Well... Too bad the blue dingy thingy isn't connected to the overhead map lights.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <BR>Left one on, the other night. Went to pull the car out today. Battery was, pretty much, a doorstop. <BR>Gave me a good excuse to go for a drive for an hour or so, tonight.<BR>Had to charge up that battery.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
